# pnpm 11 reads ONLY auth and registry settings from this file. Any other
# key here is ignored silently — no warning, no error, it simply has no
# effect. Put runtime settings in pnpm-workspace.yaml instead; the
# previous occupants of this file (enable-pre-post-scripts,
# auto-install-peers, verify-deps-before-run, confirm-modules-purge)
# now live there.
#
# https://pnpm.io/settings
#
# Registry auth belongs in ~/.npmrc, never here — this file is committed.
